{"name":"Cuban Cigar","hex":"#927247","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cigar","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cylinder of tobacco rolled and wrapped with an outer covering of tobacco leaves, intended to be smoked.","The penis. (Can we add an example for this sense?)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cigar"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cuban cigar","blocks":[{"text":"Cuban cigars are cigars manufactured in Cuba from tobacco grown within that island nation. Historically regarded as among the world's \"finest\", they are synonymous with the island's culture and contribute over one quarter of the value of all exports from the country. The filler, binder, and wrapper may come from different areas of the island, though much is produced in Pinar del Río province, in the regions of Vuelta Abajo and Semi Vuelta, as well as in farms in the Viñales region. All cigar production in Cuba is controlled by state-owned Cubatabaco. The Cuban cigar is also referred to as El Habano."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Tobacco_field_cuba1.jpg/330px-Tobacco_field_cuba1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuban_cigar","wikidata":"Q108471343"},{"title":"Cigar","blocks":[{"text":"A cigar is a rolled bundle of dried and fermented tobacco leaves made to be smoked. Cigars are produced in a variety of sizes and shapes. Since the 20th century, almost all cigars are made of three distinct components: the filler, the binder leaf which holds the filler together, and a wrapper leaf, which is often the highest quality leaf used. Often there will be a cigar band printed with the cigar manufacturer's logo. Modern cigars can come with two or more bands, especially Cuban cigars, showing Limited Edition bands displaying the year of production."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Cigar_tube_and_cutter.jpg/330px-Cigar_tube_and_cutter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cigar","wikidata":"Q1576"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Rolling_a_Cuban_Cigar.jpg/500px-Rolling_a_Cuban_Cigar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Rolling_a_Cuban_Cigar.jpg/1280px-Rolling_a_Cuban_Cigar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Rolling_a_Cuban_Cigar.jpg/500px-Rolling_a_Cuban_Cigar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Cuban cigar being hand-rolled (hecho a mano)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARolling_a_Cuban_Cigar.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Puros1.JPG/500px-Puros1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Puros1.JPG/500px-Puros1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Various brands of cigar from Cuba including Partagás, Cohiba, Montecristo, Romeo y Julieta, and Sancho Panza","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APuros1.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/ChewithCigar.jpg/330px-ChewithCigar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/ChewithCigar.jpg/330px-ChewithCigar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"According to Ernesto \"Che\" Guevara: \"A smoke in times of rest is a great companion to the solitary soldier.\"[26]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChewithCigar.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/2025-06_-_Vi%C3%B1ales%2C_Cuba_43.jpg/500px-2025-06_-_Vi%C3%B1ales%2C_Cuba_43.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/2025-06_-_Vi%C3%B1ales%2C_Cuba_43.jpg/1280px-2025-06_-_Vi%C3%B1ales%2C_Cuba_43.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/2025-06_-_Vi%C3%B1ales%2C_Cuba_43.jpg/500px-2025-06_-_Vi%C3%B1ales%2C_Cuba_43.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A sanitary license (licencia sanitaria) delivered by the Ministry of Health, shown in a tobacco plantation in Viñales to demonstrate conformity, in June 2025","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2025-06_-_Vi%C3%B1ales%2C_Cuba_43.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Fallsview_downtown_atm_currency_04.07.2012.jpg/500px-Fallsview_downtown_atm_currency_04.07.2012.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Fallsview_downtown_atm_currency_04.07.2012.jpg/1280px-Fallsview_downtown_atm_currency_04.07.2012.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Fallsview_downtown_atm_currency_04.07.2012.jpg/500px-Fallsview_downtown_atm_currency_04.07.2012.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Advertisement aimed at American tourists in Niagara Falls, Ontario, minutes away from the US–Canada border","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFallsview_downtown_atm_currency_04.07.2012.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/MuseoRegionalTuxtla_27.JPG/500px-MuseoRegionalTuxtla_27.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/